  <reporting-org ref="GB-CHC-202918" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam GB</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;Let her voice be heard&quot; Transformative Leadership of women Leaders in Nepal</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">While the Campaign will have greater emphasis and resources placed on country level change at global level the strategic programme will also support global influencing, a strong culture of programme learning, an innovative online community of practice, components of action -research and flexible funding mechanism. Activities include compelling evidence -based research,   edutainment, social and mass media messaging, public stunts, teaching and modelling positive behaviours through art, engaging and influencing key institutional stakeholders, dialogue forums for enhancing policy framework and law enforcement, partnering and supporting platforms to escalate influence, support Women&apos;s Right Organisations (WROs&apos;) agendas in Sexual and Reproductive Health Rights (SRHR) and strengthening their capacity to raise their voices, as well as capacity building to support youth clubs for empowerment. As FECM is inextricably linked with poverty and economic status, activities will also include skills development trainings for increased economic opportunities for young women.</narrative>
  </description>
